    <string name="season_about_advent">Four weeks of watchful waiting before Christmas: we prepare for Christ\'s coming at Bethlehem and at the end of time. Violet vestments; rose on Gaudete Sunday.</string>
    <string name="season_about_christmas">From Christmas Eve to the Baptism of the Lord, the Church celebrates the Word made flesh. White and gold vestments.</string>
    <string name="season_about_lent">Forty days of prayer, fasting and almsgiving from Ash Wednesday, walking with Christ toward his Passion. Violet vestments; rose on Laetare Sunday.</string>
    <string name="season_about_triduum">Holy Thursday evening to Easter Sunday: the Lord\'s Supper, his Passion and death, and the vigil of the Resurrection. The heart of the whole year.</string>
    <string name="season_about_easter">Fifty days of Easter joy, from the Resurrection to Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit descends on the Apostles. White vestments; red at Pentecost.</string>
    <string name="season_about_ordinary">The longest season: the Church follows the public life and teaching of Jesus week by week. Green vestments, the colour of growth.</string>

